
README text for the source code for AmigaPython 2.7.18

Original Amiga port through Python 2.0 by Irmen de Jong.
Updated to Python 2.7.18 by amigazen project.


Contents:
----------
 Requirements
 Installation/Build instructions
 Networking (bsdsocket.library)
 CPU / FPU notes
 Changing other compiler options
 Notes
 Contributing
 THANKS
 Disclaimer & copyright



Requirements
------------

Current primary build (see also BUILD.md in the project root):

- VBCC with PosixLib
- NDK 3.2 (include: / netinclude: assigns as per ToolKit)
- Hard disk space for a full compile
- Library files from this Source tree (Lib/) to run the interpreter

Legacy SAS/C build (still present in the tree):

- SAS/C 6.58 preferred for the classic SMAKEFILE path
- AmiTCP / bsdsocket SDK headers where networking is enabled
- LinkLib/ memory-pool objects copied to LIB: when using that SAS/C setup

I-Net225 is not supported (dropped in late classic AmigaPython).



Installation/Build instructions
-------------------------------

Preferred (VBCC / ToolKit):

	Assign Python: to this Source directory
	cd to Source/
	make -f vmakefile

This produces a test binary named Python27 in Source/.
See BUILD.md for ToolKit, optional libraries (crc.library, asl, etc.),
and clean targets.

Legacy (SAS/C):

	Copy LinkLib/ contents to LIB: if you use the memory-pool libs
	cd to the directory containing the main SMAKEFILE
	smake

The SAS/C path produces Python27_sas (see SMAKEFILE).  Ignore routine
compiler warnings unless the link fails.

After building, run the regression / Amiga tests with your new executable.
Place the binary where your Python: assign points (often renamed to
`Python` or kept as `Python27`).



Networking (bsdsocket.library)
------------------------------

By default the port expects a TCP stack that provides bsdsocket.library
(AmiTCP historically; modern stacks such as Roadshow also work).  Runtime
checks allow the interpreter to start without networking; socket-related
modules then fail until the library is available.

usergroup.library is needed for pwd / grp / crypt-style modules.

A fully "no network" SAS/C configuration historically used
SCOPTIONS_NONET / SMAKEFILE_NONET; prefer the current vmakefile options
and pyconfig.h defines for the VBCC build.



CPU / FPU notes
---------------

Out-of-the-box builds target 68020+ with FPU (68030/881 style options in
the classic SCOPTIONS).  Building for 68000/68010 requires changing CPU
and MATH options and reviewing any CPU-specific pieces (historically the
amiga crc32 assembler path).  Report issues via amigazen project if a
low-end CPU build needs more work.



Changing other compiler options
-------------------------------

VBCC: see vmakefile and pyconfig.h / Include headers.

SAS/C: SCOPTIONS, SMAKEFILE, Include/pyconfig.h (or legacy config.h),
Include/osdefs.h, Modules/config.c.  After option changes, clean and
rebuild from scratch.



Notes
-----

Amiga-specific module documentation: Amiga_Misc/Docs/ (also shipped under
Python/Docs/amiga in the distribution tree).

Builtin GUI / OS helpers:
  amiga          Dos, ASL, EasyRequest/CurrentTime/DisplayBeep, AvailMem, ...
  amigagui       Simple Intuition window (plot/line); not named simplegfx
  amigalibs      Secondary raw LVO FFI (with Tools/ConvertFD.py and
                 Lib/site-python/*lib.py). Prefer curated APIs above.
  intuition      Thin re-export of curated EasyRequest helpers (site-python)
  intuitionlib   Example ConvertFD LVO table for amigalibs (site-python)

ctypes is not enabled for classic Amiga LVOs; amigalibs fills that niche.

Language and library reference: https://docs.python.org/2.7/

Some tests fail or are skipped on the Amiga.  socket / select need
bsdsocket.library; crypt / grp / pwd need usergroup.library.

amigazen project:
  https://github.com/amigazen/amigapython/
  http://www.amigazen.com/amigapython/
  toolkit@amigazen.com



